### Behavior and reproduction

`master` is red on the `shenyu-integrated-test-http` job: `CryptorResponsePluginTest.testWhenDoesntExistFiled` fails.

Observed on the master push run for `679a9eb69cb5fc61f1ae242c8f5bdd4011ead8f7` ([job 119079963808](https://github.com/apache/shenyu/actions/runs/39554456101/job/119079963808)):

```text
[ERROR] org.apache.shenyu.integrated.test.http.combination.CryptorResponsePluginTest.testWhenDoesntExistFiled  Time elapsed: 0.016 s  <<< FAILURE!
java.lang.AssertionError:
Expected: is "10001"
     but: was null
	at org.apache.shenyu.integrated.test.http.combination.CryptorResponsePluginTest.testWhenDoesntExistFiled(CryptorResponsePluginTest.java:129)
```

The gateway response in the same run is the new configuration error:

```text
postGateway(/http/test/payment) resp({"code":-116,"message":"Please check Cryptor response plugin's [fieldNames]"})
```

### Location and cause

`11a39fda3` (#7903, "fix(cryptor): reject missing response fields") changed `CryptorResponsePlugin.fieldErrorParse` from returning the original body to throwing `ResponsiveException` with `ShenyuResultEnum.CRYPTOR_RESPONSE_ERROR_CONFIGURATION`:

```java
protected String fieldErrorParse(final String originalBody, final ServerWebExchange exchange) {
    ShenyuResultEnum resultEnum = checkErrorEnum();
    throw new ResponsiveException(resultEnum.getCode(), resultEnum.getMsg() + "[fieldNames]", exchange);
}
```

The integrated test still asserts the previous passthrough contract — that a missing field returns the original message — so it cannot pass against the new behavior:

```java
@Test
@DisplayName("return original message when request doesnt exist filed")
public void testWhenDoesntExistFiled() throws Exception {
    initSelectorAndRules(PluginEnum.CRYPTOR_RESPONSE.getName(), "",
            SINGLETON_CONDITION_LIST, buildRuleLocalDataList("data", "decrypt", FIELD.getMapType()));
    UserDTO actualUser = HttpHelper.INSTANCE.postGateway(TEST_PATH, originalBody, UserDTO.class);
    assertThat(actualUser.getUserId(), is(originalBody.getUserId()));
    assertThat(actualUser.getUserName(), is(originalBody.getUserName()));
}
```

`#7903` validated only the cryptor module's unit tests and noted that end-to-end tests were not run, so the contract change reached `master` without the integrated test being updated.

### Expected behavior / suggested repair

Update `testWhenDoesntExistFiled` to the behavior introduced by `#7903`: assert the `-116` configuration error (`CRYPTOR_RESPONSE_ERROR_CONFIGURATION`, message `Please check Cryptor response plugin's [fieldNames]`) instead of the original body, and rename the test so it no longer describes passthrough.

If the passthrough contract is instead considered still required for this route, then `#7903` needs to be narrowed or reverted — but the test and the plugin must agree either way.

`build (shenyu-integrated-test-http)` is required for the PR merge, so this failure currently blocks every open PR until it is fixed.

Related: #6476 (the issue #7903 fixed).

