Since https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/29018, we now allow the following `obj.f()` call, but we reveal a rather complex return type of `(T & A) | (T & B)`, which could be simplified to `T` (if `T: A | B`). This simplification is correct, because `(T & A) | (T & B) = T & (A | B) = T`, where the last equality follows from the fact that `T` is a subtype of `A | B`.

```py
from typing import Self

class A:
    def f(self) -> Self:
        return self

class B:
    def f(self) -> Self:
        return self

def f[T: A | B](obj: T):
    # Currently `(T & A) | (T & B)`, could be simplified to `T`
    reveal_type(obj.f())
```
