@carljm and @AlexWaygood tell me that ty no longer wants to treat classes as bivariant. But it still treats generic protocols as bivariant. This code is accepted:

```python
from typing import Protocol

class P[T](Protocol):
    pass

def f(x: P[object]):
    g(x)

def g(x: P[int]):
    f(x)
```

