### Prerequisites

- [x] I have written a descriptive issue title
- [x] I have searched existing issues to ensure the bug has not already been reported

### Mongoose version

9.11.1

### Node.js version

26.2.0

### MongoDB server version

n/a (types only)

### Typescript version (if applicable)

6.0.3

### Description

The projection-based result narrowing added in 9.11 (#15545) drops fields that are selected through a dotted inclusion path. With `{ hostname: 1, "public.title": 1 }` the result type only contains `hostname` and `_id`, so `doc.public` no longer exists, although MongoDB returns `public: { title }`. A projection that contains only dotted paths narrows to `Pick<T, never>`.

This affects both `.lean()` and hydrated results.

The cause is in `ApplyProjection` (`types/utility.d.ts`). The inclusion branch picks `Extract<DefiningProjectionKeys<Projection>, keyof T>`, and `"public.title"` is never a key of `T`.

### Steps to Reproduce

```ts
import { Schema, model } from "mongoose";

interface IDomain {
  hostname: string;
  public: { title: string; showLegal: boolean };
}

const Domain = model<IDomain>("Domain", new Schema<IDomain>({
  hostname: String,
  public: { title: String, showLegal: Boolean },
}));

async function run() {
  const lean = await Domain.find({}, { hostname: 1, "public.title": 1 }).lean();
  lean[0]!.public.title;
  // TS2339: Property 'public' does not exist on type
  // 'Pick<IDomain & { _id: ObjectId; } & { __v: number; }, "hostname"> & Pick<..., "_id">'

  const hydrated = await Domain.findOne({}, { "public.title": 1 }).orFail();
  hydrated.public.title;
  // TS2339: Property 'public' does not exist on type
  // 'Document<unknown, {}, Pick<IDomain, never>, ...> & Pick<IDomain, never> & ...'
}
run();
```

`tsc --noEmit --strict --module nodenext --target es2022 --skipLibCheck repro.ts`

### Expected Behavior

A dotted inclusion path keeps its root field in the result type, so `public` is present, either as the full subdocument type or narrowed to the selected subpaths.

Mapping each inclusion key to its root path before the `Pick` fixes it for us. We apply this as a local patch:

```diff
   type ProjectionPath<Key> = Key extends `${infer Parent}.$` ? Parent : Key;
+  type ProjectionRoot<Key> = Key extends `${infer Root}.${string}` ? Root : Key;
 ...
-          : Pick<T, Extract<DefiningProjectionKeys<Projection>, keyof T>> &
+          : Pick<T, Extract<ProjectionRoot<DefiningProjectionKeys<Projection>>, keyof T>> &
```

The exclusion branch can stay as is: a dotted exclusion such as `{ "public.showLegal": 0 }` must not omit the whole `public` field, and today it leaves `T` unchanged, which is correct, if coarse.

